if PLATFORM_EC

config PLATFORM_EC_SYSTEM_PRE_INIT_PRIORITY
	int "System pre-initialization priority"
	default 20
	range 0 99
	help
	  CROS system uses some critical data (e.g., system reset cause) for
	  initialization. We define a PLATFORM_EC_SYSTEM_PRE_INIT_PRIORITY and
	  specify system should prepare those data before this priority for the
	  following initialization. Also, chip drivers should and only initial 
	  the critical processing for system_pre_init() before
	  PLATFORM_EC_SYSTEM_PRE_INIT_PRIORITY. This config sets the system
	  pre-initialization priority. We should let the priority as higher as
	  we can.

endif # PLATFORM_EC
